✅ 1. Find Even Numbers

🎗️ 1.1 Problem Statement
You are given a List<Integer> containing positive and negative integers.
Using Java Streams, find all the even numbers from the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Preserve the original encounter order.
🔴 Return the result as a List<Integer>.

🎗️ 1.2 Input / Output

👉 Input : [10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 33, 40]
👉 Expected Output : [10, 20, 30, 40]

🎗️ 1.3 Discussion of Your Solution

List<Integer> collect = list.stream()
                            .filter(x->x%2==0)
                            .collect(Collectors.toList());

👉 How it works
🔴 list.stream() : Creates a sequential Stream from the list.
🔴 filter(x -> x % 2 == 0) : Keeps only elements divisible by 2.
🔴 collect(Collectors.toList()) : Materializes the filtered elements into a List.
🔴 Your output: [10, 20, 30, 40] is correct.

🎗️ 1.4 Time And Space Complexity
🔴 Time: O(N) : Every element potentially needs to be examined once.
🔴 Space: O(K) : Where K is the number of even elements that pass the filter.

Worst case: K = N so auxiliary/output storage can be O(N).

One important interview distinction:

The Stream pipeline itself doesn't require O(N) extra space merely because it is a Stream.
The resulting collected list requires space proportional to the number of elements retained.
